= Establishing the MCIC 

For nearly the entire month, Bill Davies, Minister of Health, has been reaching out to the CPS for their cooperation with the establishment of the Medical Care Insurance Commission (MCIC), the arms-length agency tasked with implementing the Medicare Plan. Amendments to it's establishment have mandated atleast two of the 6-8 commission members be physicians and a supporting body, the Medical Advisory Committee, whose members must be approved by the CPS. 

After receiving no response, Davies visited Harold Dalgleish's office only to be told the CPS' response was in the mail. Still, Dalgleish's letter was not received until a week after it had been dated. Given the CPS' obstinancy, Davies personally contacted "several leading physicians" to serve on the MCIC. Although some showed sympathy for the plan, none accepted for fear of provoking the wrath of their colleagues, or as some put it, the college coming down on them "like a ton of bricks". 

Bill Davies has thus established the MCIC without college agreement or representation. Donald Tansley, head of the Budget Bureau, has been selected as chair. Dr. Samuel Wolfe, assistant professor of social and preventative medicine at the University of Saskatchewan, and Dr. Orville Hjertaas who previously worked for the HSPC will fill in as the two required physicians, both ardent believers in universal healthcare. 

- @root: Let's hope this works out...